Fix four memory-safety bugs in the pre-R-1.4.0 load() readers of
saveload.c, reached by load() on any file whose magic is not RD[ABX][2-9].

The DataLoad() path (numeric magics 1971-1977) and the version-1 string
readers trust every count and index in the file:

1. DataLoad() sizes its forwarding tables from NSymbol + NSave read from
   the file.  With both zero, R_alloc(0) returns NULL and the binary
   search in OffsetToNode() dereferences OldOffset[0] (NULL read; a
   21-byte file).  Negative counts, or a sum that overflows, size the
   tables wrongly.
2. DataLoad() stores node.OldOffset[j] with j taken straight from the
   file and never compared with NTotal: a file-controlled out-of-bounds
   write (SEGV at a wild address; a 76-byte file).
3. InStringAscii(), InStringBinary() and InStringXdr() take the byte
   count from the file unchecked.  An XDR count of 0xffffffff makes
   realloc(buf, nbytes + 1) a realloc(buf, 0), which frees the static
   buffer and returns NULL; the error() that follows leaves buf
   dangling with buflen unchanged, and the next string read writes into
   freed memory (heap-use-after-free).  Smaller counts simply ask
   malloc() for up to 2 GB per string (R Bugzilla 19046 reports the
   negative and INT_MAX cases of the same field).
4. RestoreSEXP() copies a CHARSXP's bytes with strcpy() into a CHARSXP
   that RemakeNextSEXP() sized from a separate length field, so a string
   longer than its declared length overflows the object.

The fix validates each of those at the point of use: table sizes must
be non-negative and must not overflow; node indices must lie in
[0, NTotal); OffsetToNode() uses a conventional bounded binary search
that never reads an empty table; string counts must be non-negative,
below INT_MAX, and no larger than what remains of the file (fstat on
the stream, which also stops the gigabyte allocations); a CHARSXP's
string must not exceed its declared length.  DataLoad() also now
resolves the top-level node before releasing the tables it lives in,
rather than after.

    ==1==ERROR: AddressSanitizer: SEGV on unknown address 0x2000007ff2e15906
        #0 DataLoad           src/main/saveload.c:698
    ==1==ERROR: AddressSanitizer: heap-use-after-free
        #0 InStringXdr        src/main/saveload.c:1691

Found by the load target in r-devel/r-oss-fuzz (first run, 2026-10-08;
artifacts kept locally).

Upstream status: r-devel/r-svn PR #364; R Bugzilla bug 19046 (the string
readers were reported there in April 2026 with a narrower patch; this one
is being added to that report).
Delete this patch once the fix lands in R trunk (ossfuzz.sh will report
it as already-applied in the meantime, which is harmless).

